    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d205">

                <pb facs="0453" n="425" xml:id="pg425"/>

                <head>205. Telegram From the Secretary of State to the Embassy in the Republic of
                        China<anchor n="1" xml:id="d205-f1"/></head>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#italic"
                                >Washington</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1956-08-30T16:14:00-04:00"><hi rendition="#italic">August 30,
                                1956—4:14 p.m.</hi></date></dateline></opener>
                <p>170. Embtel 978.<anchor n="2" xml:id="d205-f2"/> Inform Chinese Government U.S.
                    desires position flight of Matador missiles on Taiwan. Missiles will make
                    distinct contribution toward improving defensibility Taiwan and U.S. hopes GRC
                    willing cooperate this project. If GRC agrees in principle, we will make
                    detailed proposal at early date.<anchor n="3" xml:id="d205-f3"/></p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#bold">Dulles</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
    <standOff>
        <listAnnotation>
            <note corresp="#d205-f1" n="1" type="source" xml:id="d205-f1-content">
                <p>Source: Department of State, Central Files, 711.56393/5–456. Top Secret. Drafted
                    in CA by Douglas N. Forman, cleared in CA by Clough and in FE by Sebald, and
                    approved by Robertson.</p>
            </note>
            <note corresp="#d205-f2" n="2" xml:id="d205-f2-content">
                <p><ref target="#d173">Document 173</ref>.</p>
            </note>
            <note corresp="#d205-f3" n="3" xml:id="d205-f3-content">
                <p>In telegram 209 from Taipei, September 2, the Embassy reported that the Foreign
                    Ministry agreed and welcomed the proposal to position a flight of Matador
                    missiles on Taiwan. (Department of State, Central Files, 711.56393/9–256)</p>
            </note>
        </listAnnotation>
    </standOff>
